      "message": "fix(thread): refuse a hole the program ahead has not drilled\n\nA thread mill is not centre-cutting and the thread ride feeds it down the\nhole's axis. Generate now reads each threaded hole in the stock the\nsetup's earlier operations leave standing (the drilling laws' prior grid)\nover the minor circle less one cell, never narrower than the mill, down\nto the mill's lowest point in the hole; stock standing there, or a prior\nthat cannot be judged, is refused by name. The stamp already digests the\nprogram ahead, so moving the Drill after the Thread marks it Stale.\n\nThe thread suites' fixtures move to tests/thread_support and drill the\nhole first (modelled to z 4, threaded to z 8); the M8 NC golden gains the\nDrill ahead. The Bore ride's axis entry is filed as #1036.\n\nFixes #992\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
