        "date": "2026-11-12T18:30:27Z"
      },
      "message": "test(thread): drill ahead of the thread in main's thread fixtures (#992)\n\nMerging #1005's refreshed head (upstream/main with #1205) brought two\nthread fixtures that ran a Thread op with nothing ahead; #992's law\nrefuses that hole as undrilled. Adapt the fixtures, not the law:\n\n- hole_wall_flats.rs: the Thread verdict now tap-drills the declared\n  hole (minor dia to the tenth below) to z 4 ahead of the thread, in a\n  plate whose hole is modelled to z 4. The octagon still convicts and\n  the 96-gon still verifies clean.\n- posted_gates/thread.rs: thread_verdicts builds the golden from the\n  shared thread_support fixture (drill ahead, as thread_mill.rs writes\n  it) and runs the verification gate over the whole program.\n- nc/thread_mill_m8_multi_form.nc: regenerated - main's post now ends\n  the drill cycle with G99 and a G00 to clearance.\n\nRefs #992\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
